title: '[Jeff] How can I avoid having to constantly ask you to restate things less ambiguously?'
pid: 5b98a1b6-f8df-4602-ba06-e1e41eb7b777
body: |2-
  I'm imagining some kind of adversarial review,
  but that seems hard -- if the reviewer can wander through the code
  as ambitiously as you, they won't get confused where I do,
  and there's no obvious way to make them
  know exactly what I remember.
contains:
- bba14521-9337-41e3-bf55-93e8095850c2
